      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "carryover_65",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "carryover_percentage",
            value: 40,
          },
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "ai_aggression",
            value: 1,
          },
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "carryover_bonus",
            value: "yes",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_66",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "revelation.ogg",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/fall.webp"),
            text: _("<span color=' <<'> + _Our story begins during a time of great prosperity and peace in Wesnoth. Royal armies had destroyed the undead tombs in the east. The northern orc-forts were quiet and secure. The elves in the western forest kept to their own affairs. In the south, men built new towns and farms.</span>"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_67",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/winter.webp"),
            text: _("<span color=' <<'> + _And from those young towns arose a stout-hearted peasant militia: The South Guard, stewards of peace and order on the southern frontier. _For eight years all was well, the Guard having only to quash the occasional bandit or wild creature. Perhaps the only real unease came from the Aethenwood to the west, where the elves lived in reserved aloofness, indifferent to the doings of man. Traversing their land without permission was forbidden, but the elves rarely entered the lands of men in turn.</span>"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_68",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/summer.webp"),
            text: _("<span color=' <<'> + _Over time, in the absence of pressing danger, the South Guard grew complacent and lazy. Reports to the capital slowed, and in the spring of the ninth year, ceased altogether. Displeased with the Guard’s conduct, the Crown decided to send someone to investigate...</span>"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "loyal_69",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:make_loyal",
            units: "Mari,Deoran",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "objectives",
        side: 1,
        victory: _("Move Deoran next to Mari Attack the dummy End your turn End your turn on a village Recruit some soldiers Destroy Mari’s quintain Defeat Urza Mathin"),
        defeat: _("Get yourself killed Get yourself killed Get yourself killed Get yourself killed Get yourself killed Get yourself killed Death of Deoran Death of Mari Turns run out"),
      },
